From 3d96e081bd2e538a2ee7c1b306ca5c3cdfe304bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John O'Dell <johncodell14@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:15:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Qt client: draw the map at the tileset's pixel_ratio, sharp
 on Retina

A tileset may now say pixel_ratio = 2 in its [tilespec] section: its pixels
are meant at two per screen point (192 px tiles shown as 96 point tiles).
The Qt client then keeps the map canvas at that density: the canvas is the
map widget's size times the ratio, painted into the widget's points, so on
a 2x screen every tileset pixel lands on its own screen pixel instead of a
96 px tile being doubled. Mouse positions are converted from points to
canvas pixels, map text and lines are drawn at the density, the widgets
placed from the canvas size (minimap, battle log, tile info) use points,
and the city dialog's map and the stack chooser show the units and tiles
at their point size. Tilesets without the key get 1 and draw as before.
